Map where unwanted material enters, moves and leaves (@cm-process-map: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5", #source "../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X", #clean-manufacturing "../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/foundations/Whole-and-signed-numbers.lingua#r_0SJY2JGRVTKNRYW2N2QV64WXJ7") { r_3HDYXGSDA5NAR504BAWK57VBQD
**Read:** [Contamination control engineering — Tribble and colleagues, NASA CR 4740](../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5), chapter 4; [Cleanroom programming and energy — Tschudi, Sartor and Xu](../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X), process programming.

Draw the useful process as actual contacts and transfers: incoming parts, tools, water, gas, people, packages and waste. Add exposed surfaces and periods of storage. A contaminant can arrive in a purchased item, be generated by wear, remain from cleaning or move between steps after an apparently successful inspection.

Track a defined substance or particle class through inputs, outputs and accumulation. If the tracked category changes through reaction, fragmentation or growth, include that change explicitly. Conservation of total matter does not mean that particle number or a particular molecular identity is conserved.

**Work:** Follow one object through receipt, processing, inspection and storage. Mark an introduction mechanism and a possible observation at every interface. Distinguish removing material from the product from merely moving it to a nearby surface that can release it again.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
